# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
bin/

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Node.js dependencies (for semantic-release)
node_modules/
main
tmp/
.claude/
graphify-out/

# Embargoed tickets: a live|boundary security finding stays untracked while
# local_-prefixed, independent of anyone's global excludes file (ADR 0034). The **
# covers archive/ as well, where a ticket that closes while still embargoed (dropped,
# or done with the risk accepted) keeps its prefix until the owner accepts publishing it.
docs/tickets/**/local_*
